#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0123 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "NEW with the M2-P3 ruling (Fix #304): the {<blank>, <blank>, DERIVED} shape the dossier flagged as the surprising one, pinned rather than discovered after release. PARAMTYP is Perm, so a mostly-blank column is the common real-world shape. Under include_empty=true group GLUC carries {EMPTY:2, DERIVED:1}; maxCount 2 is held by EMPTY alone, so the MINORITY - the one record that actually declares a type - is the row flagged. That is what the operator's minority rule decides; the sheet sentence is about the PARAMETER, not about a row, and this fixture is the record of the consequence."
#library standard=adamig version=1-0
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 PARAMCD=GLUC
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col PARAMTYP type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC |
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | GLUC |
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1034 | GLUC | DERIVED
